ready: 1
kind: rule
id: capture.rule.scrub
display_id: RULE-CAPTURE-SCRUB
module: capture
title: Secrets are removed before anything is stored
summary: Every capture, event, import, and seed is scrubbed of credentials and long secret-like strings before it reaches the database.
when: Text matches any secret class in the table
then: The match is replaced with a redaction mark naming its class, and the rest of the text is kept
otherwise: The text is stored as given
table:
  columns: [Class, Matches]
  rows:
    - [private key, PEM private key blocks]
    - [cloud access key, "AWS access key ids and secret keys, GCP service account private keys"]
    - [vendor token, "GitHub, Anthropic, OpenAI, Slack, Stripe, and Kernle token formats"]
    - [web token, three base64url segments starting with eyJ]
    - [auth header, Authorization and Proxy-Authorization header values]
    - [credential assignment, "assignments whose name contains KEY, SECRET, TOKEN, PASSWORD, PASSWD, or CREDENTIAL"]
    - [URL credentials, user and password inside a URL]
    - [high entropy, base64 or hex runs of 32 or more characters with high entropy]
constraints:
  - text: Binary and image content is dropped and replaced by a placeholder
    hard: true
rationale: >-
  A secret that reaches the database also reaches memories, model requests during sleep, exports,
  and the cloud. Scrubbing at the single point of entry is the only place it can be stopped for all
  of them.
